# Engine script conventions (app/scripts)

## Contract with the app
- Plain Node ESM (`.mjs`), spawned by the main process. Communicate over stdout with line protocol: `PHASE <text>`, `PROGRESS <0-100>`, `DONE <result>`; errors to stderr as `ERROR <message>` + non-zero exit (1 unexpected, 2 domain failure, 3 LLM not configured).
- Resolve the workspace dir from `process.env.BASIS_WORKSPACES_DIR` (fallback `<repo>/workspaces`) via `lib/workspace-dir.mjs` — the slug is untrusted CLI/agent input (`--slug ../../etc` must fail).
- Workspace JSON read from disk is untrusted (shareable files): always go through the `@basis/schema` `parse*` helpers, and re-validate before writing anything back.

## LLM calls
- Always go through `llm.mjs` (`resolveModel()`, `isLlmConfigured()`, `reasoningEffort()` — config resolution lives in `@basis/schema` llm-config); never instantiate a provider directly.
- Cap output: `maxOutputTokens` set explicitly. `providerOptions: { openai: { reasoningEffort: reasoningEffort() } }`. Never set `temperature` (reasoning models reject it).
- Model output is repaired, not trusted: `extractJson` → schema parse, with one retry carrying the validation errors back to the model.
- **Citations are the product**: every brief claim must quote its source verbatim; verify with `verifyQuote` and drop what fails. Deterministic metrics (x-ray numbers) are ground truth the model may not contradict.
- Diff-first to control tokens: extract Items (Risk Factors, MD&A) with `lib/filings.mjs`, never send whole filings.

## EDGAR
- All requests go through `lib/edgar.mjs`: declarative User-Agent with contact email (`BASIS_EDGAR_CONTACT`), ≥120ms between requests, on-disk caching (`BASIS_CACHE_DIR`). Respect the SEC fair-access policy — this is a shared public resource.
- One ticker failing (rate limit, network) must not sink a whole run; log `ERROR <ticker>: ...` and continue.

## Testing
- Pure logic lives in `lib/*.mjs` with a sibling `*.test.mjs` (vitest node project). Scripts themselves stay thin.
- `node --check app/scripts/<file>.mjs` before committing.
